-- Verified access details — batch 12
--
-- 7 spot(s) with records, 39 skipped. Every sourceUrl is an official
-- government, park-authority, council or fisheries-body page (CLAUDE.md content rules 1-3).
-- Apply by hand in the SQL Editor, then rebuild (migration first, then build).
--
-- sterkfontein-dam: Free State DESTEA (Department of Economic, Small Business Development, Tourism and Environmental Affairs, the provincial reserve manager) Sterkfontein Dam Nature Reserve page, read via WebFetch: about 23 km from Harrismith on the R74; slipways and boathouses; camping with ablution facilities; no shops; gate and office hours; angling among activities. The page says nothing about angling permits or rules, so none are stated. Chalet refurbishment notice deliberately left out as transient.
--
-- nahuel-huapi-trout: Parque Nacional Nahuel Huapi (national park administration) "Pesca Deportiva" page, read via WebFetch: season 1 November to 1 May inclusive; fishing permits are mandatory and personal, sold by day, week or season at local fishing shops and retailers; spinning, trolling and fly casting authorised; independent fishing or authorised park guides; full rules in the national regulation site reglamentodepesca.org.ar. The page gives no parking, release or equipment detail, so none is stated (search snippets with parking and release rules were not on this page). Existing regulations consistent ("season dates set annually") and now carry the stated dates.
--
-- loreto-yellowtail: CONANP (Mexico's national protected-areas commission) news page on the updated management programme of Parque Nacional Bahia de Loreto, read via WebFetch: the no-fishing area grew from 108.4 to 6,219.3 hectares, low-selectivity fishing gear is restricted, and jet skis/motorised water vehicles are prohibited. The page does not spell out sport-fishing rules or zoning, so none are stated; the record tells anglers to check the zoning. The spot is written as "if fishing inside the park" since the spot location was not matched to the park boundary.
--
-- lake-biwa-bass: Shiga Prefecture page on the Invasive Alien Species Act and the ban on releasing invasive fish, read via WebFetch (Japanese): the Shiga Prefecture Lake Biwa Leisure Use Appropriateness Ordinance prohibits releasing black bass and bluegill; caught fish should be taken to the designated recovery boxes or holding pens around the lake; transporting them live within Lake Biwa (including harbours) to a recovery box or keeping them alive in a bucket while fishing is allowed, but taking live fish out of the lake area is a violation. The page itself notes the national Act does not directly ban catch-and-release and leaves release bans to local governments. CONTRADICTION FIXED: existing regulations said "Transporting live bass is illegal"; too broad, so reworded.
--
-- hokkaido-shiretoko-salmon: Hokkaido Prefecture fisheries management page "Fishing rules and manners", read via WebFetch (Japanese): dedicated salmon/trout fishing rules and a list of zones near river mouths where salmon and trout may not be taken, regional rule maps and warnings on illegal gear. Existing regulations already say river salmon fishing is prohibited; the addition is the prohibited zones near river mouths (prefecture list). The bear-related request to keep out of Horobetsu River estuary areas came from the Shiretoko Foundation (not a government body) and is not used.
--
-- okinawa-gt: Okinawa Prefecture FAQ page on harvesting marine animals and plants (Japanese), read via WebFetch: ordinary (recreational) people may use rod and hand-line fishing (no lights), landing nets, cast nets from shore only, hand-held spears without propulsion, hand capture and trolling; spearfishing with mechanical propulsion is banned; fragments of coral and live rock may only be taken with permission; harvesting protected coral species is forbidden; some areas and periods are closed to harvesting and the Water Products Division (098-866-2300) publishes a pamphlet. Existing regulations (no licence, reef protection, typhoon season) consistent. The Yaeyama spawning closure seen in a search result was not on this page and is NOT stated (the spot is not tied to Yaeyama).
--
-- volga-delta-catfish: Rosrybolovstvo (Federal Agency for Fisheries), Volga-Caspian territorial administration, "Pamyatka dlya rybolova-lyubitelya" for Astrakhan Oblast, read via WebFetch (Russian): amateur fishing on public water bodies is free and without charge under the Volga-Caspian fishing rules; fishing is prohibited 16 May-20 June across the region (except within settlements); sturgeon species are prohibited; prohibited zones include the Volga pre-mouth protected area, sturgeon and fish spawning grounds, hydro-facility safety zones and registered shipping channels; nets, traps and similar gear banned. The page's species list was machine-summarised inconsistently (zander appeared in one listing), so NO species other than sturgeon is stated, and the 2026 roach/vobla bans are not restated. CONTRADICTION/GAP FIXED: existing regulations did not mention the regional closed period or the prohibited zones.
--
