UPDATE public.spots SET access = '{"shore":true,"boat":true,"ramp":"Slipways and boathouses are available at the reserve","facilities":["Caravan park with ablution facilities and power points","Shoreline camping sites without electricity"],"notes":"Sterkfontein Dam Nature Reserve lies about 23 km from Harrismith on the Harrismith/Bergville road (R74). The reserve''s gate is open 06:00 to 22:00 and its office 07:30 to 16:00. There are no shops on the reserve, so bring your own provisions. DESTEA lists angling among the reserve''s activities but its page does not state permit requirements: contact the reserve on 058 622 3520 and check current Free State fishing rules before you go.","sourceUrl":"https://www.destea.gov.za/?page_id=3974"}'::jsonb, updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'sterkfontein-dam';

UPDATE public.spots SET access = '{"shore":true,"boat":true,"notes":"The Nahuel Huapi National Park administration states that the fishing season runs from 1 November to 1 May inclusive. Fishing permits are mandatory and personal, available by the day, the week or for the season from local fishing shops and retailers, and each permit comes with its own specific regulations. Spinning, trolling and fly casting are the authorised methods. You can fish independently or with an authorised park guide. The park directs anglers to the national fishing regulation site (reglamentodepesca.org.ar) for current rules.","sourceUrl":"https://nahuelhuapi.gov.ar/pesca-deportiva/"}'::jsonb, regulations = '["Nahuel Huapi National Park licence required — separate from the provincial licence","Park season runs from 1 November to 1 May inclusive — check the park administration for the current season and rules","Catch-and-release and barbless rules apply in much of the park"]'::jsonb, updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'nahuel-huapi-trout';

UPDATE public.spots SET access = '{"boat":true,"notes":"If fishing inside Parque Nacional Bahia de Loreto, note that CONANP''s updated management programme enlarged the park''s no-fishing area to 6,219.3 hectares, restricts low-selectivity fishing gear and prohibits jet skis and other motorised water vehicles. Check the park''s current zoning map and CONANP and CONAPESCA rules before fishing.","sourceUrl":"https://www.gob.mx/conanp/prensa/conanp-actualiza-el-plan-de-manejo-del-parque-nacional-bahia-de-loreto?idiom=es"}'::jsonb, updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'loreto-yellowtail';

UPDATE public.spots SET access = '{"shore":true,"boat":true,"facilities":["Designated invasive-fish recovery boxes and holding pens around the lake"],"notes":"Shiga Prefecture''s Lake Biwa leisure ordinance prohibits releasing black bass and bluegill anywhere in the prefecture. Caught fish should be taken to the designated recovery boxes or holding pens set up around the lake. Moving them live inside the Lake Biwa area to a recovery box, or keeping them alive in a bucket while you fish, is allowed, but taking live fish out of the lake area is a violation. Check Shiga Prefecture''s current guidance on recovery-box locations before fishing.","sourceUrl":"https://www.pref.shiga.lg.jp/ippan/kankyoshizen/biwako/13517.html"}'::jsonb, regulations = '["A yugyoken permit is required for parts of the lake — check with the local cooperative","Largemouth bass is a designated invasive species in Japan; releasing it alive is prohibited in Shiga under the prefecture''s Lake Biwa ordinance","Do not transport live bass away from Lake Biwa — take caught fish to a designated recovery box or holding pen, or follow Shiga Prefecture''s disposal guidance"]'::jsonb, updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'lake-biwa-bass';

UPDATE public.spots SET access = '{"shore":true,"boat":true,"notes":"Hokkaido Prefecture publishes fishing rules that include a list of zones near river mouths where salmon and trout may not be taken, regional rule maps, and warnings about illegal gear and methods. Check the prefecture''s current list and the Shiretoko-area rule map before fishing for salmon from shore or boat, and follow park guidance on brown bears.","sourceUrl":"https://www.pref.hokkaido.lg.jp/sr/ggk/ggs/turi-r-m/rule-manner.html"}'::jsonb, regulations = '["No licence for sea fishing, but river salmon fishing is generally prohibited in Hokkaido","Salmon and trout may not be taken in designated zones near river mouths — check the Hokkaido Prefecture list and regional rule maps","Brown bears are present; never fish alone and follow park guidance"]'::jsonb, updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'hokkaido-shiretoko-salmon';

UPDATE public.spots SET access = '{"shore":true,"boat":true,"notes":"Okinawa Prefecture allows recreational anglers to use rod and hand-line fishing (without lights), landing nets, cast nets from shore only, hand-held spears and trolling. Spearfishing with mechanical propulsion is banned, harvesting protected coral is forbidden, and taking coral fragments or live rock needs permission. Some areas and periods are closed to harvesting, and the prefecture''s Water Products Division (098 866 2300) publishes a pamphlet of the rules. Check the prefecture''s current rules and closed areas before fishing.","sourceUrl":"https://www.pref.okinawa.jp/shigoto/suisangyo/1011042/1011071.html"}'::jsonb, updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'okinawa-gt';

UPDATE public.spots SET access = '{"boat":true,"notes":"Rosrybolovstvo''s Volga-Caspian administration states that amateur fishing on public water bodies in Astrakhan Oblast is free and needs no permit, but fishing is prohibited across the region from 16 May to 20 June (except within settlement boundaries). Sturgeon species are prohibited. Fishing is not allowed in the Volga pre-mouth protected area, on sturgeon and other spawning grounds, in hydro-facility safety zones or in registered shipping channels, and nets, traps and similar gear are banned. Check the current Volga-Caspian basin rules and species bans before fishing.","sourceUrl":"https://vktu.fish.gov.ru/pravila-rybolovstva/pamyatka-dlya-rybolova-lyubitelya/"}'::jsonb, regulations = '["No general recreational licence is required on public water bodies in Astrakhan Oblast","Amateur fishing is prohibited across the region from 16 May to 20 June (except within settlement boundaries), and sturgeon are strictly protected — targeting or keeping them is a serious offence","Prohibited zones include the Volga pre-mouth protected area, spawning grounds, hydro-facility safety zones and shipping channels; some delta channels are within protected reserves — check the current Volga-Caspian rules"]'::jsonb, updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'volga-delta-catfish';

